Package: ldfreq
Type: Package
Title: Reproducible Lexical Diversity and Frequency Profiles
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person(
        given = "Ryuya",
        family = "Komuro",
        email = "komuro.4121@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
Description: Compares lexical diversity and reference-vocabulary profiles while
    retaining the formula, parameters, preprocessing choices, and match coverage
    used in each analysis. Computes twelve lexical-diversity measures from
    ordered tokens or raw English text; compares selected Maas and MTLD
    definitions; and exposes local MATTR windows. Bundled New JACET 8000 and
    TUBELEX tables support lexical-level coverage and corpus-relative frequency
    profiles, with off-list terms and non-computable requests kept explicit.
    Additional functions provide exact lexical overlap, reference-set coverage,
    caller-supplied word-family, lexical norm and adjacent n-gram frequency profiles,
    descriptive comparisons of scored
    vocabulary response pairs, multi-document workflows, and plots.
    Bundled MorphoLex English worksheets provide derivational morphology
    reference data under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (noncommercial use).
    Nation's BNC/COCA Level 6 word-family lists are bundled under CC BY-SA 4.0.
    A local MorphyNet reader retains derivational relations and source identity.
    External annotations, local MASC Penn annotations and optional 'quanteda' integration retain
    supplied token boundaries and source positions for corpus analysis.
    Contextual review connects caller-supplied lexical candidates and explicit
    decisions to keyword-in-context displays and original text.
    External model outputs can be attached with checked source identities
    while keeping model suggestions separate from reviewer decisions.
    The methods include Covington and McFall (2010)
    <doi:10.1080/09296171003643098> and McCarthy and Jarvis (2010)
    <doi:10.3758/BRM.42.2.381>.
